findings.body:
The PR says it makes `read_parquet` read only the columns a chain uses. This diff also does three other things:
- adds `adbc-driver-sqlite` as a mandatory runtime dependency for every install;
- adds a new subprocess-based ADBC writer (`sqlite_arrow.py`, `SQLiteWarehouse.arrow_writer`) that writes to the live warehouse file from a second SQLite library;
- changes how all Arrow UDF output is encoded and stored.

These change how every tabular load writes data and add a native binary dependency. None of that is needed to project columns. If this work belongs to the stacked base PR (#2225), it should be reviewed and merged there, not hidden in this diff. Otherwise, split it out or explain it in the description.
